      "speaker": null,
      "text": "11–16 The content is repeated from earlier in the chapter, but note the presence of second aorists – ἔδακε (second aorist of δάκνω), ἤρου (second aorist of ἐρωτάω), ἐλάβετε (second aorist of λαμβάνω), ἐγένετο (second aorist of γίγνομαι), and ἔθετε (aorist of τίθημι, a verb which you have not yet learned in detail).\n18 εἶδον ἰδ- is the second aorist stem of ὁράω.\n19–20 πόθεν ὢν τυγχάνεις ‘Where do you happen to come from?’\n27 ἐξευρίσκεις εὑρίσκω has perfect tense ηὕρηκα, familiar from Archimedes’ cry on discovering the principle of displacement. Second aorist stem εὑρ- is met in the next line.\n29–30 ἔμαθον, ἔτυχε Second aorists respectively of μανθάνω, τυγχάνω.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
